  "description": "A fast breakdown of The Basal Ganglia: Habits and Movement for builders.",
  "is_free": false,
  "published": true,
  "story": {
    "hook": {
      "text": "You don't think about how to walk. Your basal ganglia automated that skill long ago.",
      "visual": "🚶"
    },
    "buildup": {
      "text": "This group of nuclei deep in the brain manages voluntary movement and habit formation.",
      "visual": "🔄"
    },
    "discovery": {
      "text": "When you repeat an action enough, the basal ganglia take over so the cortex can focus elsewhere.",
      "visual": "🎯"
    },
    "twist": {
      "text": "In Parkinson's disease, dopamine-producing cells here die, making simple movements agonizingly difficult.",
      "visual": "🤲"
    },
    "climax": {
      "text": "The same circuitry that automates tying your shoes also drives addictive behaviors.",
      "visual": "🔁"
    },
    "punchline": {
      "text": "Habits live in the basal ganglia—good ones and bad ones alike.",
      "visual": "⚙️"
    }
  },
  "quiz": {
    "question": "What role do the basal ganglia play?",
    "options": [
      "Managing habits and voluntary movement",
      "Processing emotions",
      "Regulating body temperature"
    ],
    "correct": 0
  },
